  "question": {
    "text": "A variable line through the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> cuts the coordinate axes at the points <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> respectively. If the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> divides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> internally in the ratio <math><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the equation of the locus of <math><mi>P</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the&nbsp;equation of <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> which passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math><br />Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then</p><p><math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> &amp; <math><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi></math> &amp; <math><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> locus of <math><mi>P</mi></math> is <math><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math></p>"
  }
